## OPTIONS

What the statement selected. Each option is labelled with its kind: **Recommended (SHOULD)**, which a server may decline with a warning row; **Optional (MAY)**, behaviour the release leaves to the implementation; or **Spec defect**, an option only because the released text is defective. The statement selects one arm of each, and the other arms are skipped.

### EHR

#### COMPOSITION

| Option | Kind | Selected arm | Passed | Failed | Warning | Errored | Skipped |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| `etag-sent` | Recommended (SHOULD) | `etag-declined`, nothing to run | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| `composition-xml-read` | Optional (MAY) | `xml-supported` | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| `flat-format` | Optional (MAY) | not selected |  | | | |  |
| `ehr-status-flat` | `@SpecDiverge` | `flat-served` | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 |
| TRIAL text | BASE on TRIAL text | | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 |

<details>
<summary>What these options decide</summary>

- **`etag-sent`** (Behaviour the release leaves open): Whether the server supports etag-sent.
- **`composition-xml-read`** (Canonical XML): Whether the server supports composition-xml-read.
- **`flat-format`** (Simplified Formats and Web Template): Whether the server supports flat-format.
- **`ehr-status-flat`** (Simplified Formats and Web Template): Whether the server supports ehr-status-flat. Upstream report [#352](https://github.com/Vernum-Projecten/Veredictum/issues/352): EHR\_STATUS has no flat form (confirmed).
- **TRIAL text**: BASE cases whose cited text the release marks TRIAL. They are read with the options and never count in the BASE tally.

</details>

